# ShieldWise — Environment Variables
#
# This project is a single self-contained static HTML file with no backend,
# no build step, and no server-side code. It does not use, require, or read
# any environment variables — there is nothing to configure here.
#
# The two external endpoints the site talks to are NOT secrets:
#   1. A Google Form embed URL (public by design — that's what an embedded
#      form is meant to be).
#   2. A Google Sheet published-to-web CSV link (public by design — "Publish
#      to web" explicitly creates a public, read-only link with no auth).
# Both are hardcoded in index.html because they are meant to be public, the
# same way a public form or public dataset link would be.
#
# If you later add a real backend, a paid API, or anything requiring a secret
# key, put the variable names (not the values) here, e.g.:
#
# SOME_API_KEY=
#
# and load the real value from your hosting platform's own environment
# variable settings (Vercel/Netlify project settings) — never commit the
# actual key to this repository.
